1
00:00:02,238 --> 00:00:08,319
On Sunday morning, Mr. and Mrs. Arable and Fern were sitting at breakfast in the kitchen.

2
00:00:08,319 --> 00:00:13,439
Avery had finished and was upstairs looking for his slingshot. "Did you know

3
00:00:13,439 --> 00:00:16,000
that Uncle Homer's goings had hatched?"

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,679
asked Fern. "How many?" asked Mr.

5
00:00:19,679 --> 00:00:26,399
Arable. "Seven," replied Fern. "There were eight eggs, but one egg didn't

6
00:00:26,399 --> 00:00:34,000
hatch, and the goose told Templeton she didn't want it anymore, so he took it away."

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,640
"The goose did what?" asked Mrs.

8
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:42,479
terrible, gazing at her daughter with a queer, worried look, "Told Templeton she

9
00:00:42,479 --> 00:00:49,279
didn't want the egg anymore," repeated Fern. "Who is Templeton?" asked Mrs.

10
00:00:49,279 --> 00:00:52,719
Arable. "He's the rat," replied Fern.

11
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:56,960
"None of us like him much." "Who's us?"

12
00:00:56,960 --> 00:01:02,960
asked Mr. Arable. "Oh, everybody in the barn cellar. Wilbur and the sheep and

13
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:10,079
the lambs and the goose and the gander and the gosslings and Charlotte and me.

14
00:01:10,079 --> 00:01:17,520
Charlotte said Mrs. Arable. Who's Charlotte? She's Wilbur's best friend.

15
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:20,399
She's terribly clever.

16
00:01:20,399 --> 00:01:22,960
What does she look like? asked Mrs.

17
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:31,279
Arable. Well, uh, said Fern thoughtfully. She has eight legs. All spiders do, I guess.

18
00:01:31,279 --> 00:01:37,840
Charlotte is a spider?" asked Fern's mother. Fern nodded. "A big gray one.

19
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:42,719
She has a web across the top of Wilbur's doorway. She catches flies and sucks

20
00:01:42,719 --> 00:01:47,359
their blood. Wilbur adores her."

21
00:01:47,359 --> 00:01:53,920
"Does he really?" said Mrs. Arable rather vaguely. She was staring at Fern

22
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:56,719
with a worried expression on her face.

23
00:01:56,719 --> 00:02:03,039
Oh yes, Wilbur adores Charlotte, said Fern. Do you know what Charlotte said

24
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:09,198
when the gosslings hatched? I haven't the faintest idea, said Mr. Arable. Tell

25
00:02:09,198 --> 00:02:14,960
us. Well, when the first go stuck its little head out from under the goose, I

26
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:22,640
was sitting on my stool in the corner and Charlotte was on her web. She made a speech.

27
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:28,399
She said, "I am sure that every one of us here in the barn seller will be

28
00:02:28,399 --> 00:02:33,520
gratified to learn that after four weeks of unremittent effort and patience on

29
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:38,640
the part of the goose, she now has something to show for it." "Don't you

30
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:44,560
think that was a pleasant thing for her to say?" "Yes, I do," said Mrs. Arable.

31
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:51,119
"And now, Fern, it's time to get ready for Sunday school. and tell Avery to get ready.

32
00:02:51,119 --> 00:02:55,520
And this afternoon, you can tell me more about what goes on in Uncle Homer's

33
00:02:55,520 --> 00:03:01,279
barn. Aren't you spending quite a lot of time there? You go there almost every

34
00:03:01,279 --> 00:03:06,719
afternoon, don't you? I like it there, replied Fern. She wiped her mouth and

35
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:12,158
ran upstairs. After she had left the room, Mrs. Arable spoke in a low voice

36
00:03:12,158 --> 00:03:20,079
to her husband. I worry about Fern, she said. Did you hear the way she rambled

37
00:03:20,079 --> 00:03:25,520
on about the animals, pretending that they talked?

38
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,319
Mr. Arable chuckled.

39
00:03:28,319 --> 00:03:35,359
"Maybe they do talk," he said. "I've sometimes wondered. At any rate, don't

40
00:03:35,359 --> 00:03:41,520
worry about Fern. She's just got a lively imagination. Kids think they hear

41
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:48,238
all sorts of things." Just the same, I do worry about her, replied Mrs. Arable.

42
00:03:48,238 --> 00:03:53,920
I think I shall ask Dr. Doriap about her the next time I see him. He loves Fern

43
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:58,319
almost as much as we do, and I want him to know how queerly she's acting about

44
00:03:58,319 --> 00:04:04,640
that pig and everything. I don't think it's normal. You know perfectly well

45
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:08,560
animals don't talk. Mr. Arable grinned.

46
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:15,399
Maybe our ears aren't as sharp as ferns, he said.

47
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:18,079
Chapter nine.

48
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:21,960
Wilbur's boast.
